{"id": "EUVD-2026-101237", "enisaUuid": "80e83ff9-6ad9-3574-a722-7d6e5ede5159", "description": "Dromara Skyeye through commit 65d3ddcede70 contains an sql injection vulnerability that allows authenticated low-privileged users to inject SQL via the keyword parameter in the queryErpOrderItem MyBatis statement using raw ${} substitution. Attackers can send crafted keyword values to the queryWarehousingDetails or queryOutgoingDetails endpoints to extract database data, including other tenants' data, using boolean, UNION, error or time-based techniques.", "datePublished": "2026-10-14T14:16:50", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-14T16:20:46", "baseScore": 7.1, "baseScoreVersion": "4.0", "baseScoreVector": "CVSS:4.0/AV:N/AC:L/AT:N/PR:L/UI:N/VC:H/VI:N/VA:N/SC:N/SI:N/SA:N", "references": ["https://hackmd.io/@1ExmmukzRMWN7B4gQ4W-4Q/skyeye-erp-statistics-keyword-sqli", "https://github.com/dromara/skyeye/blob/65d3ddcede701d33ea5416e47c9b656e47d56401/skyeye-erp/erp-pro/src/main/resources/mapper/erp/StatisticsMapper.xml#L29-L31", "https://github.com/dromara/skyeye/blob/65d3ddcede701d33ea5416e47c9b656e47d56401/skyeye-erp/erp-pro/src/main/java/com/skyeye/controller/StatisticsController.java#L33-L45", "https://github.com/dromara/skyeye", "https://www.vulncheck.com/advisories/dromara-skyeye-through-commit-65d3ddcede70-sql-injection-via-keyword-parameter"], "aliases": ["CVE-2026-110609", "GHSA-wg4g-q6wc-f4xf"], "assigner": "VulnCheck", "epss": 0.47, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "cf59b356-7d28-32b2-a359-7deca693b00f", "product": {"name": "skyeye", "vendor": {"name": "dromara"}}, "product_version": "0 \u226465d3ddcede701d33ea5416e47c9b656e47d56401"}], "enisaIdVendor": [{"id": "b3ccb07a-c4ab-305b-a475-ca9636f60d36", "vendor": {"name": "dromara"}}], "isExploited": false}